  "rationale": "**Mechanism.** `discovery::used_plugins` returns the canonical ids of the loaded plugins whose manifest name an applicable `use` entry names (`PluginsConfig::is_used_in` -> `used_names_in(workspace_root)` -> `name_matches`, compared under the owning PM's rule, so a registry plugin matches exactly). Each caller puts that set in `PredicateContext::with_used`, and `Plugin::applies` lets a `requires_use` plugin past the dormancy check only when `ctx.is_used(&self.canonical)`. The callers are `sync` (skills and MCP), `help_render::render_help`, `subcommand_dispatch::dispatch_external`, `status_command`, and in `hook.rs` `dispatch_plugin_hooks`, `prewarm_hook_sources` and `discovery_hint`; `plugins::active_plugins` seeds the active set through `record_active`, which calls `applies`.\n\n**Tests (all pass, re-run this pass).** `discovery::tests::use_wakes_a_registry_plugin_only_by_its_exact_name` checks that `use = [\"my-plugin\"]` puts the dormant registry plugin's id in `used_plugins`, and that `my_plugin` does not. `use_wakes_and_remove_sleeps_a_dormant_plugin` (tests/enablement.rs) runs `cargo agents use gateless-plugin` and finds the dormant plugin's skill installed, then reaped after `use --remove`. `plugins_entries_match_registry_plugin_names_exactly` checks that the exact spelling wakes it. These tests cover only sync (skills) inside a workspace, with a dormant plugin that has no plugin-level predicates.\n\n**Why false: two cases where an applicable `use` entry names a dormant registry plugin and it stays inactive.**\n\n1. **Outside a workspace.** The chapter defines an unscoped entry as applicable. But `dispatch_external`, `render_help`, `dispatch_plugin_hooks`, `prewarm_hook_sources` and `discovery_hint` all compute `used` as `workspace.as_ref().map(|ws| used_plugins(..)).unwrap_or_default()`. When no package manager finds a project, `used` is empty and a global `use` wakes nothing. Registry plugins still load and activate there: I checked this with the prebuilt binary, using a scratch `SYMPOSIUM_HOME` that has a path registry and `use = [\"sleepy\"]`. In a directory with no `Cargo.toml`, `cargo agents star-cmd` (from a `depends-on = [\"*\"]` plugin) ran, but `cargo agents sleepy-cmd` (from the dormant, globally `use`d plugin) failed with `no plugin defines subcommand`. The same command ran inside a cargo project.\n2. **Non-dependency plugin predicates.** A registry plugin whose only plugin-level gate is `env(...)`, `shell(...)` or `path_exists(...)` is dormant, because `requires_use` counts only dependency mentions and custom predicates. After the `is_used` check, `Plugin::applies` still evaluates `self.manifest.predicates`. With `use = [\"envy\"]` and `predicates = [\"env(UWD_NOT_SET)\"]`, `cargo agents status` reported `envy` as `dormant: awaiting cargo agents use`: inactive even though a `use` entry names it. This may be intended, since the plugin's own gate still applies, but the requirement as written says `use` MUST activate it. A maintainer has to either reword the requirement or change the code.\n\nHook dispatch and the help path outside a workspace were judged from code, not tested; I saw the subcommand path's behavior directly.",
  "requirement": "Symposium MUST activate a dormant registry plugin while an applicable `[plugins] use` entry names it."
